# --- Terraform (applies to both terraform/core/ and terraform/alerts/) ---
# Local provider cache and state — state lives remotely in omotayotfstate,
# never locally. Pattern matches both directories since .gitignore rules
# apply relative to wherever the matched path appears in the repo tree.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars.json
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
# --- Terraform variable files ---
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored, in either
# terraform/core/ or terraform/alerts/ — committed for reproducible
# provider version resolution across machines/CI runs.

# --- Helm / Grafonnet ---
# Chart.lock and the pinned kube-prometheus-stack .tgz ARE committed
# (see DECISIONS.md — ArgoCD needs no live network access to the
# upstream Helm repo at sync time). Only the Jsonnet vendor/ library
# source is excluded — regeneratable via `jb install`, and not
# meaningfully reviewable as a diff.
charts/*/dashboards/jsonnet/vendor/
# jsonnetfile.lock.json IS committed, for the same reproducibility
# reason as .terraform.lock.hcl and Chart.lock.

# --- Secrets / local overrides ---
# None of this project's real secrets should ever be typed into a
# committed file — Key Vault + CSI is the actual mechanism — but this
# is a blanket guard against an accidental local override slipping in.
*.local.tfvars
.env
.env.*

# --- Screenshots working folder ---
# If you keep a scratch/raw-capture folder before curating final
# screenshots into the repo's screenshots/ folder, exclude the scratch
# one specifically here (adjust name to whatever you actually use).
screenshots/raw/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp